    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.05.95": {
      "title": "Tier 2 Canada Research Chair, Social Innovation and Entrepreneurship and Director",
      "description": "Tier 2 Canada Research Chair, Social Innovation and Entrepreneurship and Director - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Tier 2 Canada Research Chair, Social Innovation and Entrepreneurship and Director Maria T. Schneider Social Innovation Institute, Triffo School of Business Competition No. 26.05.95 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Tenure-Track. Commensurate with qualifications and experience. A review of applications will begin July 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Tenure-Track. Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Closing Date A review of applications will begin July 15, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University’s Triffo School of Business is seeking applications for a Tier 2 Canada Research Chair (CRC) in Social Innovation and Entrepreneurship and Director of the Maria T. Schneider Social Innovation Institute. The position will commence January 1, 2027, or as close to that date as mutually agreed, subject to final budgetary approval. This position will support and build on MacEwan University’s Teaching Greatness: Strategic Vision 2030 The CRC will build on the Triffo School of Business’ strengths in community-driven social innovation, transforming ideas into action and community impact. The successful applicant will receive a full-time, probationary tenure-track position (at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor) and may be rooted in any of the four Departments in the Triffo School of Business. See our website Triffo - MacEwan University for information on the Departments . The successful applicant will also serve as the Director of MacEwan’s Maria T. Schneider Social Innovation Institute. Upon starting the academic appointment, the successful applicant will work with the University to apply for a Tier 2 Canada Research Chair. For further information relating to a Tier 2 Chair, please click here . In addition to establishing a research program, the workload includes teaching and curriculum development, as well as contributions to university service. The successful applicant will have a reduced teaching load during the CRC appointment. MacEwan University, in the heart of downtown Edmonton, leads with our Teaching Greatness: Strategic Vision 2030, dedicated to providing students with a transformative, academically rigorous, and personal learning experience in a creative, collaborative, and supportive learning environment. MacEwan continues to evolve and adapt to meet the changing needs of its students and the communities it serves, and today MacEwan offers student-focused instruction and inspires students through a powerful combination of academic excellence and personal learning opportunities. The Schneider Institute will be housed in MacEwan’s new academic building, scheduled to open in Winter 2027. The Schneider Institute supports the entire entrepreneurial ecosystem from idea generation to commercialization and the implementation and scaling of ideas into a business enterprise. The Schneider Institute is an important hub for students, faculty members, and community partners to collaborate on social innovation and scale ideas into social enterprises. As part of its leadership in innovative teaching and research, the Schneider Institute serves as a space to facilitate ideation and convenes events to develop tools and approaches to support innovation. Among the Institute’s interests are community-driven innovation and scaling up innovative ideas to drive entrepreneurial growth among disadvantaged and marginalized groups. As Director, your responsibilities will include leading the Schneider Institute in meeting and growing its mandate, managing students and research personnel, and fundraising and managing a budget to support its activities. Candidates with experience or interest in researching Indigenous business will have many opportunities at MacEwan University. Edmonton has the second-largest urban Indigenous population in Canada, and MacEwan University has many Indigenous business partners and opportunities to connect with Indigenous communities and businesses. In addition, MacEwan University’s Indigenous Center, kihêw waciston, is a home away from home for Indigenous students and offers support for gathering, working, and growing in a community that honors the distinctive knowledge of Indigenous peoples. As a successful applicant, you will have: A PhD in business, management, or a related field; Evidence of outstanding teaching ability, and a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching; and, An active program of original and innovative academic research in innovation, entrepreneurship, social enterprises, and/or Indigenous business, or a related field, and evidence of a research program and research productivity. You should submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements of a Tier-2 CRC, a curriculum vitae, a statement of research interests, including how they align with the CRC focus, and a teaching dossier (including your teaching philosophy and recent teaching evaluations). The cover letter should indicate in which of the Triffo School of Business’ four Departments you would seek an appointment. CRC Eligibility Criteria A Tier-2 CRC has a term of five years, which may be renewed once for a second five-year term. Tier 2 Chairs are intended for exceptional emerging scholars. Candidates must be ten years or less from their first independent academic research-related appointment at the time of nomination. Applicants who are more than 10 years beyond their first independent academic research-related appointment, and who have career breaks, such as maternity, parental, or extended sick leave, clinical training, etc., may have their eligibility for a Tier 2 Chair assessed through the program’s Tier 2 justification process. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity, and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.240": {
      "title": "Dean, Triffo School of Business",
      "description": "Dean, Triffo School of Business - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Dean, Triffo School of Business Triffo School of Business Competition No. 26.09.240 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Commensurate with qualifications and experience. The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity Guided by Teaching Greatness: Strategic Vision 2030 , MacEwan is focused on exceptional undergraduate teaching and bold innovation. With over 21,000 students enrolled across over 55 programs of study in four faculties and two schools, the University offers a connected, learner-centred culture that emphasizes critical thinking, community-based learning, and high-quality student support. Recently renamed in recognition of a transformative gift from entrepreneur and community leader Ron Triffo, the Triffo School of Business is a dynamic and growing business school at MacEwan University. Distinguished by its entrepreneurial spirit, strong undergraduate focus, and deep connections to the Edmonton business community, the School offers a comprehensive portfolio of degree, diploma, and certificate programs that prepare students to lead, innovate, and create value in a rapidly evolving global economy. Accredited by the European Foundation for Management Development (EFMD), the School combines academic rigor with practical, real-world learning opportunities that connect students with industry, community, and experiential learning. Building on a proud history of graduate success and supported by a highly engaged community of faculty, staff, alumni, and partners, the School is entering an exciting new phase of growth. The opening of the new 35,000-square-metre Triffo School of Business building in January of 2027 will further enrich MacEwan's vibrant downtown campus, creating dynamic spaces for learning, collaboration, innovation, and community engagement while supporting the School's continued growth and impact across Edmonton, Alberta, and beyond. Reporting to the Provost & Vice-President, Academic, the Dean provides strategic, academic, and operational leadership to one of MacEwan University's largest and fastest-growing academic units. The Dean will advance a compelling vision for the School that builds on its reputation for teaching excellence, student success, community engagement, and growing scholarship. As a member of the University's senior leadership team, the Dean will guide the School through a period of significant growth and transformation, strengthening its academic programs, fostering excellence in teaching, experiential learning, and research, and championing a culture that is collaborative, inclusive, and student-centred. A visible and engaged ambassador for the School, the Dean will cultivate meaningful relationships with industry, government, alumni, donors, and community partners to enhance the School's profile and reputation. As a champion for the Triffo School of Business, the Dean will articulate a compelling vision for the School, amplify its distinctive strengths, and strengthen its brand and reputation as a leading business school with deep connections to industry and community. The successful candidate will have a strong record of teaching, scholarship, and service to qualify for an appointment as a full professor; with a demonstrated record of progressive leadership experience within a complex university environment. They will be a strategic and future-focused leader who can advance long-term priorities, identify opportunities for growth and partnership, and guide a dynamic School through growth and change while building trust, alignment, and a strong sense of community. The ideal candidate will lead with integrity, foster meaningful relationships, communicate with authenticity and transparency, and effectively advocate for the interests of the School and University. With strong strategic and financial acumen, exceptional communication skills, and a deep commitment to student success, and faculty and staff engagement, the next Dean will drive innovation, elevate the School's distinctive reputation and external profile, and position the Triffo School of Business for continued success and impact. How to Apply MacEwan University has partnered with Andrea Patrick and Cora Hui of Odgers to support this recruitment for an existing position. The ideal start date is summer 2027. Applications are encouraged immediately and should be submitted online at https://careers.odgers.com/en-ca/32011. The Committee's consideration of applications will begin in late November. The position will remain open until filled. For more information, or to submit a nomination, please reach out to TriffoDean@odgers.com . Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.237": {
      "title": "Director, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Director, Alumni Engagement - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Director, Alumni Engagement Advancement, University Relations Competition No. 26.09.237 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $117,979 to $159,492 per annum October 14, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $117,979 to $159,492 per annum Closing Date October 14, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Director, Alumni Engagement for a full-time continuing opportunity with our Advancement department. In this role, you will oversee the university’s outreach and programming for a growing community of nearly 100,000 MacEwan alumni. As a member of the Advancement leadership team, you will lead a team responsible for developing and delivering strategies, programs, services, events, and activities that foster meaningful, lifelong relationships between the university and its alumni. Working in partnership with the Director, Philanthropy, you will also contribute to the strategic direction and overall effectiveness of the department while leading an integrated engagement strategy that strengthens alumni participation, stewardship, volunteerism, advocacy, and philanthropic support. Key responsibilities include: Providing strategic leadership for the university's alumni relations function and establishing a long-term vision for alumni engagement that supports institutional priorities, enhances alumni affinity, and strengthens the university's reputation and community impact; Developing and executing an integrated alumni relations strategy aligned with the university's strategic plan, Advancement priorities, and broader University Relations objectives; Identifying opportunities to enhance the university's profile, expand alumni participation, and strengthen relationships that contribute to long-term institutional success; Cultivating strategic partnerships across the university to embed alumni engagement within institutional initiatives, academic priorities, student success efforts, experiential learning opportunities, and community engagement activities; Representing the university externally with alumni, community organizations, professional associations, volunteers, and external partners to strengthen relationships and advance institutional priorities; Collaborating with the Director, Philanthropy to ensure alignment between alumni engagement activities and Advancement priorities by identifying opportunities that support stewardship, advocacy, and philanthropic participation; Leading, managing, and developing the Alumni Relations team to deliver high-quality programs, services, communications, events, volunteer engagement, and relationship-building activities that strengthen alumni affinity, participation, and connection to the university; In consultation with the AVP, Advancement, planning, forecasting and managing the alumni annual budget, including tracking and controlling all expenditures within assigned budget; Promoting alumni achievements, contributions, and success stories to strengthen institutional reputation, alumni pride, and community connection; Overseeing alumni events, reunions, networking opportunities, mentorship initiatives, affinity programs, awards programs, and recognition activities; Serving as the primary staff liaison to the Alumni Association and Alumni Advisory Council, providing strategic guidance, fostering effective relationships, and supporting the achievement of annual priorities and objectives; and Overseeing the administration and continuous improvement of alumni leadership structures, charters, policies, and practices that support effective alumni participation and representation. Skills You will have: Strong leadership and people management skills, including the ability to recruit, develop, coach, motivate, and lead high-performing teams; Strong relationship-building, collaboration, and influencing skills, with the ability to establish credibility and work effectively with senior leaders, faculty, staff, alumni, volunteers, donors, community partners, and other stakeholders; Excellent written, verbal, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with diverse audiences and represent the university professionally; The ability to engage, influence, and support volunteer leaders, advisory councils, and alumni leadership groups in achieving shared objectives; Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills, with the ability to assess complex issues, balance competing priorities, and develop practical solutions; The ability to use data, performance measures, and stakeholder feedback to inform planning, evaluate outcomes, and support continuous improvement; Knowledge of relationship management principles, stakeholder engagement practices, volunteer leadership, and alumni engagement strategies within a complex organizational environment; The ability to exercise sound judgment, diplomacy, discretion, and political acuity when navigating sensitive, confidential, or high-profile matters; and The ability to manage multiple priorities, lead change, and adapt strategies in response to evolving organizational needs and stakeholder expectations. Qualifications A minimum of an undergraduate degree in Communications, Marketing, Business, Public Relations, or a related discipline. A minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible experience in alumni relations, advancement, stakeholder engagement, external relations, communications, volunteer management, community engagement, or related field. A minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible leadership experience, including direct responsibility for staff, budgets, and program delivery within a complex organization. Experience developing and implementing engagement, relationship-building, or outreach strategies involving diverse stakeholder groups and competing priorities. Experience leading volunteer engagement programs, advisory bodies, boards, councils, committees, or other governance-related structures would be considered an asset. Experience within a post-secondary institution, not-for-profit organization, membership-based organization, or similarly complex stakeholder environment would be considered an asset. The completion of professional development or certification in fundraising, advancement, volunteer management, leadership, or stakeholder engagement would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out of Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.242": {
      "title": "Director, Health, Safety and Environment",
      "description": "Director, Health, Safety and Environment - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Director, Health, Safety and Environment Health Safety and Environment Competition No. 26.10.242 Posting Date October 6, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $117,979 to $159,492 per annum October 25, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $117,979 to $159,492 per annum Closing Date October 25, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Director, Health, Safety and Environment for a full-time continuing opportunity with our Health, Safety and Environment department. Are you a visionary health, safety, and environmental leader who is passionate about building a culture where people can learn, work, and thrive safely?  We are seeking a strategic and collaborative Director, Health, Safety and Environment (HSE) to provide institution-wide leadership for health, safety, environmental, and biosafety programs. Reporting to the Senior Director, Campus Safety and Security, you will shape and advance the University's vision for health, safety, and environmental stewardship by strengthening governance, accountability, compliance, and risk management frameworks across a diverse and dynamic academic environment. You will serve as a trusted advisor to senior leadership, guiding the institution through emerging risks, regulatory requirements, and opportunities to enhance organizational performance and sustainability. In this influential role, you will lead a multidisciplinary HSE team and drive initiatives that foster shared responsibility, leadership accountability, and the integration of HSE principles into strategic planning, operations, research, and decision-making. Through strong partnerships with internal and external stakeholders, you will champion a proactive, risk-informed approach that supports the University's commitment to safe, healthy, compliant, and sustainable learning and working environments. Key responsibilities include: Providing strategic leadership for the University’s health, safety, environmental, and biosafety (HSE) programs, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities, divisional goals, and the University’s strategic direction; Championing a culture of health, safety, environmental stewardship, and shared accountability by embedding HSE principles into academic, research, administrative, and operational activities across the University; Establishing and maintaining governance frameworks, policies, standards, controls, and performance measures that promote accountability, regulatory compliance, operational excellence, and continuous improvement; Providing expert strategic advice and recommendations to senior leadership on emerging risks, legislative and regulatory developments, institutional priorities, and opportunities to strengthen HSE performance and risk management practices; Overseeing institutional compliance with applicable federal and provincial legislation, regulations, permits, licenses, standards, and reporting requirements, ensuring effective systems, processes, controls, and assurance mechanisms are in place; Serving as the University’s designated authority for regulated biosafety and pathogen-related activities, ensuring compliance with applicable legislation, permits, licenses, and regulatory reporting requirements; Leading the identification, assessment, mitigation, monitoring, and reporting of health, safety, environmental, and biosafety risks to protect people, property, research activities, and the environment; Overseeing significant incidents, investigations, inspections, audits, regulatory matters, and corrective action programs, ensuring root causes are addressed and organizational learning is achieved; Monitoring HSE performance by analyzing key performance indicators, incident trends, audit findings, compliance outcomes, stakeholder feedback, organizational risk data, and other relevant insights; Leveraging data, technology, and continuous improvement methodologies to strengthen HSE programs, optimize service delivery, enhance the accessibility and effectiveness of HSE services, and drive strategic improvements; Representing the University with regulatory agencies, government bodies, auditors, professional associations, and external stakeholders, fostering positive relationships and supporting organizational credibility and compliance; Overseeing institutional HSE communications and engagement strategies to ensure messaging is clear, consistent, timely, and aligned with regulatory requirements and organizational priorities; Providing regular reports and strategic recommendations to senior leadership regarding HSE risks, compliance status, program effectiveness, and progress toward departmental and institutional objectives; and Exercising delegated authority to address serious or imminent HSE risks, including directing corrective actions, restricting activities, or recommending the suspension of work to protect the health and safety of the University community and the environment. Skills You will have: Advanced knowledge and expertise in occupational health and safety, environmental, biosafety, fire and life safety programs, including applicable legislation, regulations, standards, and compliance requirements; The proven ability to interpret complex regulatory requirements, assess institutional risk, and provide practical, risk-informed advice to senior leaders; Strong knowledge of HSE management systems, governance frameworks, incident management, corrective actions, and continuous improvement practices; Demonstrated leadership experience building and managing high-performing HSE teams, setting priorities, shared accountability, allocating resources, and delivering service excellence; Recognized for developing trusted partnerships across diverse stakeholder groups and positioning HSE as a strategic advisor to the organization; Exceptional communication and influencing capabilities, with a talent for translating technical and regulatory information into clear, actionable guidance; Advanced analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to evaluate trends, compliance data, audits, incidents, and emerging risks to inform decision-making; Judicious decision-making and professional credibility in managing sensitive, complex, and high-risk issues with operational, regulatory, and reputational implications; The ability to manage competing priorities, respond effectively to emerging challenges, and make timely, risk-based decisions in a dynamic environment; Well-developed project and change management skills, including leading organization-wide initiatives, program enhancements, and process improvements; Expertise in risk assessment, hazard identification, root cause analysis, program evaluation, compliance monitoring, and corrective action planning; and The confidence to represent University before regulators, auditors, professional organizations, and external partners, while maintaining credibility and advancing organizational objectives. Qualifications A minimum of a degree in occupational or environmental health and safety, or a related field. A minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible experience in health, safety, and environment, including experience with and responsibility for institutional HSE programs, regulatory compliance, risk management, incident response, and service delivery, ideally within a university, public sector, or similarly complex institution. A minimum of 5 years of experience in a health and safety leadership role, including responsibility for leading staff, programs, service delivery, and institution-wide HSE initiatives. Experience fostering a strong safety culture through education, engagement, accountability, and leadership development. Previous experience working in a post-secondary or other public sector environment would be considered a strong asset. A relevant professional designation from the Board of Canadian Registered Safety Professionals, Board of Certified Safety Professionals, or Canadian Registration Board of Occupational Hygienists would be considered a strong asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out-of-Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.247": {
      "title": "Director, Security Operations and Emergency Management",
      "description": "Director, Security Operations and Emergency Management - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Director, Security Operations and Emergency Management Campus Safety and Security Competition No. 26.10.247 Posting Date October 9, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $117,979 to $159,492 per annum October 26, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $117,979 to $159,492 per annum Closing Date October 26, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Director, Security Operations and Emergency Management for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Campus Safety and Security department. Reporting to the Senior Director, Campus Safety and Security, you will provide operational leadership for campus security, emergency management, dispatch, preparedness, and incident response. Working within the portfolio’s strategic direction, you will translate priorities into effective operational plans, service standards, procedures, training, and response frameworks that support a safe, secure, and resilient campus. Leading the Security Operations and Emergency Management team, you will foster accountability, operational excellence, readiness, and continuous improvement. Through strong partnerships across the university and with external agencies, you will strengthen campus safety and resilience while serving as the critical link between strategic priorities and frontline operations. In this role, you will ensure teams have the clarity, resources, and tools required to respond effectively to risks, incidents, and emerging challenges with confidence and effectiveness. Key responsibilities include: Leading and developing Security Operations and Emergency Management teams, fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, service excellence, and continuous improvement; Overseeing the delivery of security operations, dispatch services, emergency preparedness, incident response, and emergency management programs; Directing operational planning, resource allocation, workforce planning, budgeting, and performance management to ensure effective and sustainable service delivery; Building and maintaining strong partnerships with university stakeholders, emergency responders, government agencies, and community partners to advance campus safety and preparedness; Providing leadership and support during significant incidents, emergencies, and Emergency Operations Centre activations, ensuring effective coordination and response; Overseeing security systems, risk assessment processes, crime prevention initiatives, safety awareness programs, and emergency preparedness training; Monitoring operational performance, analyzing trends and emerging risks, and implementing improvements that enhance service quality, readiness, and resilience; Ensuring compliance with legislation, regulatory requirements, university policies, and industry best practices related to security and emergency management; and Leading continuous improvement activities, including audits, exercises, after-action reviews, and policy and procedure development to strengthen operational effectiveness. Skills You will have: Advanced knowledge of security operations, security methodology, community policing principles, incident response, crime prevention, dispatch services, emergency management, and operational risk mitigation in a complex institutional environment; Strong working knowledge of applicable federal, provincial and municipal legislation and regulations; Proven leadership and people management skills, including the ability to lead through direct report managers who oversee supervisors and frontline teams; The established competence to set clear expectations, support manager decision-making, monitor performance, address operational issues, and promote accountability, consistency, and service quality; Excellent problem-solving and risk assessment skills, with a proven ability to identify, assess and mitigate threats and risks; The validated capability to manage sensitive, complex, or time-sensitive operational matters using sound judgment, discretion, procedural fairness, and appropriate escalation; The ability to communicate clearly and effectively with managers, supervisors, frontline staff, institutional partners, external agencies, and community members during routine operations, incidents, and emergency situations; Demonstrated effectiveness to build and maintain effective operational relationships with internal partners, law enforcement, emergency response agencies, social service agencies, post-secondary security colleagues, vendors, and community safety partners; Strong organizational and time management skills, including the ability to manage competing operational priorities, respond to emerging issues, and meet deadlines in a dynamic environment; and The demonstrated commitment capability to be firm, calm, fair, authoritative, and service-focused when responding to incidents, leading teams, resolving issues, and engaging with members of the campus community. Qualifications A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in Criminology, Social Sciences, Public Administration, or related field. Currently or previously holding a Alberta Peace Officer appointment, or the eligibility to obtain an Alberta Peace Officer appointment within six (6) months of hire. A minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible experience in security operations, public safety, law enforcement, peace officer operations, or a related operational environment, including at least 5 years in a management role. Certified Protection Professional (CPP) or Physical Security Professional (PSP) designation. Emergency management training or certification, such as Incident Command System training. A valid Standard First Aid and CPR certification. Experience working in a public sector, post-secondary, or similarly complex institutional environment would be considered an asset. Experience managing financial and human resources within approved authority would be considered an asset. Experience managing staff in a unionized environment would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The successful incumbent will be required to obtain a Police Record Check with a Vulnerable Sector Check at their own cost. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out of Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.201": {
      "title": "Vice-President, Finance & Administration and Chief Financial Officer",
      "description": "Vice-President, Finance & Administration and Chief Financial Officer - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Vice-President, Finance & Administration and Chief Financial Officer Office of Vice President, Finance and Administration Competition No. 26.08.201 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Commensurate with qualifications and experience. The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity Reporting directly to the President and Vice-Chancellor, the Vice-President, Finance & Administration and Chief Financial Officer (VPFA & CFO) is a key member of the Executive Council and a strategic leader. As a trusted strategic advisor to the President, the Board of Governors, and the executive leadership team, the VPFA & CFO plays a central role in shaping MacEwan University's future by providing strategic financial leadership that enables institutional growth, advances academic priorities, and strengthens long-term sustainability. As the University's senior finance executive, the Vice-President, Finance & Administration provides strategic leadership that strengthens financial sustainability, drives enterprise transformation, and enables long-term institutional growth. This is an exceptional opportunity to lead a broad and impactful portfolio spanning finance, information services, human resources, and facilities and sustainability services. As MacEwan's senior financial executive, the VPFA & CFO will contribute to enterprise-wide strategy, champion operational excellence, lead transformative initiatives, and identify innovative approaches to revenue generation, resource optimization, and long-term financial resilience. With responsibility for financial stewardship, enterprise risk management, capital planning, strategic resource allocation, and the systems that support these functions, the VPFA & CFO will help position the University for its next phase of growth and success. Working closely with students, faculty, staff, government, unions, and community partners, the VPFA & CFO will help shape an institution with significant momentum, ensuring MacEwan University continues to deliver an exceptional student experience while achieving its bold ambitions for the future. Ideal Candidate Profile Success in this role requires more than financial expertise. It calls for a collaborative, forward-thinking leader who thrives in complex environments, builds trusted relationships across diverse constituent groups, and inspires innovation and continuous improvement. The ideal candidate is an accomplished executive who combines strategic vision with sound judgment, collaborative leadership, and exceptional relationship-building skills. They will bring deep financial expertise, a strong record of leading complex organizations through growth and change, and the ability to serve as a trusted advisor on financial stewardship, enterprise risk, governance, and institutional strategy. They combine strategic vision with exceptional financial acumen and are recognized for challenging assumptions, identifying opportunities, and delivering meaningful organizational change. They have demonstrated success leading enterprise-wide transformation across finance, human resources, information technology, and other administrative functions, building integrated teams that work collaboratively toward shared institutional outcomes rather than operating in functional silos. A confident and forward-thinking leader, they inspire trust through integrity, transparency, and accountability while fostering a culture of innovation, continuous improvement, and evidence-informed decision-making. They are an effective collaborator who builds strong relationships across diverse constituent groups and thrives in complex, highly regulated environments. The successful candidate will be passionate about developing people, building organizational capacity, and helping position MacEwan University for continued success and long-term impact. Experience & Qualifications Recognizing that no one candidate is likely to meet all of the following qualifications in equal measure, the following experience and qualifications are desirable and will be used in the assessment of candidates for the position: Relevant university degree required and Chartered Professional Accountant (CPA) designation highly preferred. Equivalent senior financial leadership experience as the organization's chief financial executive may be considered. Significant executive leadership experience leading finance within a large, complex organization, preferably in the post-secondary sector. Demonstrated success leading enterprise transformation, organizational redesign, technology-enabled modernization, and continuous improvement initiatives. Demonstrated success leading finance and administrative functions, including financial stewardship, budgeting, forecasting, enterprise risk management, and organizational transformation. Demonstrated success leading multidisciplinary portfolios that include finance, human resources, information technology and other corporate services. Experience providing strategic advice to executive leadership and boards within complex governance environments. Proven ability to lead multidisciplinary portfolios and build high-performing teams through periods of growth and change. How to Apply To learn more about this opportunity or to request a copy of the Executive Brief, contact Katherine Frank ( kfrank@kbrs.ca ) or Beth McLennan ( bmclennan@kbrs.ca ). Completed applications can be submitted online using the \"Apply Now\" button on the KBRS website: https://www.kbrs.ca/Career/17871607893690000008msq . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. KBRS and MacEwan University will provide support in the recruitment processes to applicants with disabilities, including accommodation that takes into account an applicant’s accessibility needs. If you require accommodation in order to participate as a candidate in the recruitment process, please contact accommodate@kbrs.ca . Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.241": {
      "title": "Accounting Technician ll",
      "description": "Accounting Technician ll - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Accounting Technician ll Accounts Payable, Financial Services Competition No. 26.10.241 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week) October 18, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week) Closing Date October 18, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Accounting Technician II to join our Accounts Payable (AP) team of the Shared Services Centre (SSC), a department within Financial Services. This full-time continuing position supports the university by providing accounts payable expertise and a strong commitment to the delivery of service excellence. As an Accounts Payable Accounting Technician II, you will report to the Accounts Payable Supervisor and be primarily responsible for accurate and timely processing of assigned supplier invoice and voucher processing, ensuring compliance with policy and procedures, participating in regulatory accounting period activities, building and maintaining strong business partnerships with key stakeholders, and providing outstanding customer service excellence. This is an exciting opportunity to work in a collaborative and service-focused environment. If you are keen, motivated and eager to learn, we encourage you to apply today! Key responsibilities include: Invoice, Voucher and Payment Management Review and verify supplier invoices for timely and accurate payment with a three-way match process; ensuring proper authorizations, supporting documentation and compliance; Timely and accurate entry of supplier invoices for payment processing; Processing journal vouchers and voucher corrections; and Monitor payment schedules to ensure timely disbursements. Customer Service & Support Provide customer service support and expert advice to MacEwan stakeholders on accounts payable processes; Collaborate with purchasing and receiving departments to resolve invoice or purchase order concerns; Serve as the primary contact for assigned supplier inquiries regarding payment and account status; Build and maintain positive business partnerships with suppliers and internal stakeholders; Participate in team meetings and proactively identify opportunities to improve business processes; and Cross train on other operational and accounting functions to support departmental objectives within the SSC as required and directed by the Senior Manager, SSC. Reconciliation, Records and Compliance Reconcile supplier statements and resolve outstanding balances or discrepancies; Assist in month-end and year-end close activities by performing monthly account reconciliations and journal entries; Ensure compliance with financial policies, operational procedures, and best practices; Maintain organized and accurate records of invoices, payments, and correspondence using a digital file system; and Support internal and external audits by providing requested documentation and information. Skills You will have: Excellent verbal and written communication and keen emotional intelligence skills; Strong critical thinking, investigative and analytical skills with an aptitude for identifying key issues and problem solving; The ability to effectively organize, prioritize, and manage time to meet deadlines; Strong attention to detail and initiative to maintain accurate and thorough quality of work; A collaborative service-focused mindset with the ability to interact, build and maintain positive working relationships with a wide variety of stakeholders in a professional, respectful and courteous manner; Strong self-motivation with the ability to work effectively under pressure, adapt to changing priorities, and remain calm and professional; Work effectively in a collaborative and fast-paced team environment as well as independently; A compliance-focused mindset with strong working knowledge of accounts payable internal controls, policy and procedure interpretation, and the application of best practices; and High motivation to learn new skills and tasks. Qualifications A minimum of an Accounting or Business Administration diploma. A minimum of three (3) years of accounts payable experience in a high-volume accounting environment. Solid understanding and experience in completing account reconciliations and financial analysis. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, SharePoint, Outlook.) Working knowledge of PeopleSoft Finance and Supply Chain Management system particularly as it pertains to the Accounts Payable module, is considered an asset. Knowledge of industry best practices and business processes is considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.222": {
      "title": "Advisor, Procurement and Contracts",
      "description": "Advisor, Procurement and Contracts - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Advisor, Procurement and Contracts Procurement and Contract Management Services Competition No. 26.09.222 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week). MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week).​ October 12, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week). Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week).​ Closing Date October 12, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Advisor, Procurement and Contracts for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Procurement and Contract Management Services. The Advisor, Procurement and Contracts is responsible for leading assigned end-to-end low to medium-risk, low to medium-visibility, and/or low to medium-value procurement and contract services to meet the widely varying needs of the stakeholders across the university. Key responsibilities include: Planning and Research Conducting regular meetings with internal stakeholders to understand procurement and business requirements; and Completing market research, procurement background assessment, and recommending procurement and contracting strategies to best meet business objectives with leadership support. Competitive Bidding and Contract Administration Providing procurement and contract advice to various MacEwan’s stakeholders while working closely with MacEwan's legal department for expertise; Full ownership of the bidding process, which includes document development, solicitation on Alberta Purchasing Connection (APC), evaluation,  awards on APC, regrets, and debriefs while ensuring proper stakeholder engagement, Leading end-to-end low to medium-risk, low to medium-visibility, and/or low to medium-value RFx processes; Sporadic involvement in high value/risk/visibility contracts and competitive bids under supervision, or in a supporting role to Procurement Senior Advisors; Leading and facilitating debriefing of unsuccessful bidders toward improvement of future responses and, based on feedback received, improvement of future competitive bidding documents.; Interpreting contract requirements, terms & conditions, and ensuring that all parties understand their responsibilities; and Facilitating and managing internal and external stakeholders’ engagement during the competitive bid and contract administration. Departmental and Business Support Acting as a liaison between internal stakeholders and suppliers as needed; and Diligently moving the business forward by suggesting process improvements, mitigating risks to the university, and containing costs. Skills You will have: Exceptional attention to detail; The ability to identify risks and propose strategies to mitigate same in the contracting process; Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and projects; Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written; Strong interpersonal, analytical and organizational skills; Demonstrated ability to deliver services in a service-oriented and client-centered environment; High level skill in using computers including experience with standard business applications including Microsoft Office and Excel; Demonstrated ability to work as a strong contributor in a team environment and able to effectively interact with all levels of management and staff; Experience with Contract Management Database, preferably PeopleSoft FSCM modules such as e-procurement, procurement, and PO Contract; Knowledge of relevant legislation and trade agreements with respect to public procurement obligations; Knowledge and experience in applying principles of project management; and Knowledge of contract laws. Qualifications A minimum of a post-secondary certification in a business-related field. A minimum of 5 years' related procurement experience. A minimum of 3 years supporting competitive bid processes, writing resultant contracts based on an existing contract template. Experience working in post-secondary institutions or public procurement would be considered an asset. Experience using MS Access, SharePoint, Visio, and / or Project. Formal training in Business (contract law) or public procurement would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. ​ ​ This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. ​ All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.205": {
      "title": "Finance and Accounting Technician",
      "description": "Finance and Accounting Technician - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Finance and Accounting Technician Academic Affairs, Faculties of Health and Community Studies and Nursing Competition No. 26.08.205 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). October 9, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band D (Steps 1-8): $28.501 - $41.449 per hour. $51,872 - $75,438 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date October 9, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Finance and Accounting Technician for a full-time continuing position within Academic Affairs. Reporting to the Finance Officer, you will provide a range of support services to your portfolio of clients, ensuring their financial needs are met through tracking, reporting, reconciling financial reporting information, administering project grants, and assisting with other processes as needed. This position portfolio includes the Faculty of Health and Community Studies as well as the Faculty of Nursing. Key responsibilities include: Performing reconciliation of financial information and preparing journal entries; Preparing reports, pivot tables, and tracking sheets; Assisting with operating and capital budgets preparation; Answering finance-related staff and vendor inquiries; Following financial processes and statements to ensure compliance with professional accounting standards, contractual, legislative obligations, and organizational financial reporting requirements; Reviewing and tracking various financial accounting procedures and workflows to ensure that potential problems or concerns are addressed immediately; Preparing and ensuring the accuracy and timely submission of various transactions including fund transfers, journal entries, invoices, and purchase requisitions; Preparing and reviewing reports with budget holders, monitoring budgets and account balances and investigating discrepancies; Performing initial report analysis to support various financial management systems; Documenting processes that support efficient transaction flow, appropriate internal control, and compliance with university financial policies, procedures, and timelines; Reviewing capital asset requirements with programs and assisting with procurement and management of assets; Participating in asset counting where needed and reviewing asset records for accuracy, actioning asset transfers or disposal as needed; and, Other duties as assigned. Skills You will have: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with a keen attention to detail; Excellent verbal and written communication skills, for effective communication in writing, in person, and during presentations; Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to adapt to changing priorities with tight deadlines; The ability to work independently as well as within a broader team; Knowledge of accounting principles and financial reporting; Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and in data analytics; and, The ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise discretion, and tact. Qualifications A minimum of a diploma in Finance, Accounting, or related discipline. A minimum of 3 years of related experience. Experience processing a variety of financial transactions. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.223": {
      "title": "Organizational Design and Job Evaluation Consultant",
      "description": "Organizational Design and Job Evaluation Consultant - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Organizational Design and Job Evaluation Consultant Human Resources Competition No. 26.09.223 Posting Date October 9, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) $84,387 to $113,923 per annum October 9, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary $84,387 to $113,923 per annum Closing Date October 9, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking an Organizational Design and Job Evaluation Consultant for a full-time continuing opportunity with our Human Resources department. Reporting to the Director, Organizational Design and Development, you will work to improve organizational effectiveness through the development, project management, analysis, and implementation of organizational and job design solutions and job evaluation activities at MacEwan University. Key responsibilities include: Continuously building and maintaining relationships with senior leaders and clients to understand business needs and strategic goals; Developing and maintaining institutional standards and guidelines for organizational and job design best practices; Acting as a subject matter expert and influencer in providing organizational design expertise and advice to assist leaders in implementing and managing organizational structures and systems that foster excellence and equity; Conducting internal and external scans to support evidence-based organizational design decision-making; Designing new jobs and redesigning existing jobs in order to improve role clarification, work coverage, and succession opportunities, taking into consideration job evaluation implications; In collaboration with Human Resources Business Partners, developing organizational review implementation plans, including phasing, impact analysis, communications, and change management; Conducting detailed stakeholder assessments and job audits to ascertain change impacts and needs, to tailor messages, actions, and approaches to different audiences; Maintaining internal equity through the delivery of job evaluation using the University's designated job evaluation plan(s) and Job Families Framework for MacEwan Staff Union and Out of Scope positions; Leading and/or participating in projects that ensure the effectiveness of job evaluation program delivery such as benchmarking, evaluation plan updates/maintenance, and developing informational resources; Providing training and communications about compensation, job design, and evaluation processes to the MacEwan community; Evaluating and adjudicating job evaluation appeals, and handling grievances related to job evaluation issues which includes working collaboratively with Human Resources Business Partners when required; and Liaising and working with MacEwan Staff Union representatives on job evaluation issue resolution, answering inquiries, and providing information when required. Skills You will have: Excellent analytical and evaluative skills; Client focus with the ability to develop effective partnerships; The ability to foster and maintain relationships with senior leadership, operational managers, a wide variety of staff, union representatives, as well as team members; The ability to advise on effective strategies for organizational and job design, transformation, and alignment; The ability to work well under pressure with minimal supervision; Strategic thinking, innovation and influencing skills; The ability to thrive in ambiguous and complex situations, as well as adapt to an ever-changing environment; Communication, change management, interpersonal, organizational and negotiation skills; Consulting, coaching, and group facilitation skills; The ability to lead project implementation and effectively assess risk, readiness, and resistance; The ability to foster an inclusive and welcoming environment to support productive discussions, robust expression of ideas, group dialogue, and decision making; and Proficiency utilizing the Microsoft Office Suite. Qualifications A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in human resources, commerce, or a related discipline. A minimum of 5 years of related experience, including the development and delivery of organizational design projects, programs, policy and services, as well as in applying job evaluation systems and practices. Experience applying current knowledge of theory and practice related to organizational and job design, job evaluation and related impact assessments and change management. Experience using an HRIS system such as PeopleSoft would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Out of Scope employee policy (D1015). Applications sourced through this process may be considered for similar opportunities within MacEwan University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.206": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Project Coordinator - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Project Coordinator School of Continuing Education Competition No. 26.08.206 Category Salary Closing Date Part-Time Non Recurring Term (less than 35 hours per week) MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $47,106 - $68,493 per annum (Based on 28 hours per week). The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Part-Time Non Recurring Term (less than 35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $47,106 - $68,493 per annum (Based on 28 hours per week). Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Project Coordinator for a part-time (0.8 FTE) 15-month, non-recurring term opportunity with the School of Continuing Education. The Project Coordinator is responsible for coordinating the planning, organization, and delivery of projects that advance the School of Continuing Education’s (SCE) strategic goals. Under the direction of the Senior Business Development Officer, the Project Coordinator translates established project goals and priorities into actionable project plans and ensures activities remain aligned with defined outcomes. You will manage project plans, schedules, budgets, and documentation, facilitating communication among internal and external stakeholders, and supporting quality assurance, reporting, and evaluation. By applying project management best practices, you will help ensure that projects are delivered on time, within scope and budget, and in alignment with institutional policies and stakeholder requirements. Where projects are grant-funded, the role also coordinates compliance, reporting, and financial accountability activities to ensure projects meet funding requirements and deliverables. Key responsibilities include: Coordinating activities, timelines, and roles with multiple stakeholders; Breaking down major deliverables into manageable components, integrating milestones into project schedules, and monitoring progress against agreed deadlines; Coordinating the people, materials, and services required to achieve project outcomes and program development goals; Tracking and reporting on budgeted spending, grants, and/or inventory to support accountability and transparency; Coordinating procurement of external services, consultants, SMEs, and other project resources in accordance with university processes; where applicable, ensuring alignment and compliance with funding agreements and guidelines; Organizing and facilitating meetings, preparing agendas, records decisions, and following up on action items; Managing communication protocols (e.g., shared calendars, resource repositories, process maps) to ensure clarity and accountability among internal and external stakeholders; Managing events, focus groups, and sector consultations; Preparing and maintaining accurate project documentation, including contracts, agreements, meeting minutes, records, and progress updates; Preparing status updates, briefing notes, presentations, updates, and final reports for leadership and stakeholders; and Collaborating and communicating effectively with all project stakeholders with an appropriate cadence. Skills You will have: Strong project coordination skills with a solid understanding of project management principles, methods, and techniques; The ability to navigate and coordinate multistakeholder projects; The ability to define and refine project requirements throughout the project lifecycle, ensuring clarity and alignment with outcomes; Demonstrated ability to problem-solve, assess situations, think critically, and apply sound judgment in making timely and informed recommendations; Strong collaboration and communication skills; Strong analytical and decision-making skills with keen attention to detail and accuracy; The ability to navigate sector-specific communications, spaces, and networks; The ability to develop trust by consistently displaying honesty, integrity, and ethical conduct in all interactions, fostering credibility, accountability, and strong working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders; The ability to identify, assess, and mitigate risks related to project scope, timelines, funding requirements, and deliverables; Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate complex information, prepare reports, and tailor messaging to diverse audiences; Demonstrated self-motivation and initiative, effectively working independently while collaborating productively within a team environment to achieve shared goals and deliver results; Strong interpersonal, collaboration, and conflict resolution skills that enable positive and productive stakeholder relationships; Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to adapt to shifting priorities, manage multiple deadlines, and maintain focus under pressure; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and collaboration platforms; and Experience using Asana, Hubspot, SIS and Outlook, Sharepoint and Teams would be considered an asset. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, or related field. A minimum of 3 years of project coordination experience, preferably in a post-secondary or public sector environment. Demonstrated experience coordinating projects with multiple stakeholders. Experience with budget tracking and reconciliation. Experience or knowledge of the transportation sector would be considered an asset. Experience working on multi-stakeholder projects would be considered an asset. Experience with grant-funded projects, compliance reporting, or government funding agreements would be considered an asset. Experience supporting program or curriculum development projects would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.238": {
      "title": "Supervisor, Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Supervisor, Student Recruitment – International - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Supervisor, Student Recruitment – International Office of the University Registrar Competition No. 26.09.238 Posting Date October 2, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band F (Steps 1-8): $36.722 - $53.420 per hour. $66,833 - $97,225 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). October 19, 2026 Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band F (Steps 1-8): $36.722 - $53.420 per hour. $66,833 - $97,225 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date October 19, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Supervisor, Student Recruitment – International for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Office of the University Registrar (OUR). Reporting to the Manager, Student Recruitment, you will be accountable for the planning, implementation, and evaluation of MacEwan University’s student recruitment activities focused on international markets. You will play a key role in the development of strategies and initiatives to strengthen the university’s brand, attract and recruit future students, and achieve application and new student enrolment goals set out in the University's strategic enrolment management plan. You will also provide day-to-day operational leadership and supervision of the international student recruitment team and oversee the educational agent portfolios. Key responsibilities include: Assisting the Manager in the development of short and long-term international recruitment strategies, including targeting by country, program and agent for the beginning of fall and winter terms; Ensuring that recruitment goals set by senior administration are achieved; Measuring effectiveness of recruitment activities by developing and maintaining a system to capture and analyze statistical and database information by country, program, and educational agent in conjunction with Institutional Analysis & Planning (IAP); Supervising and guiding a team of international student recruiters; by assigning, distributing, reviewing, organizing, coordinating, and prioritizing workloads; Monitoring assignments, deadlines, and ensuring goals and objectives are met in alignment with quality and quantity standards; Serving as a point of contact, reference and escalation for the team; Working with international student recruiters to discuss problems, providing solutions and advice, and removing barriers to success through active problem-solving, based on knowledge of established processes, practices and standards; Undertaking recruitment activities in select countries as required; Collaborating with educational agents and high schools to promote MacEwan University as a choice destination; and Conducting appropriate post trip follow up with educational agents and schools ensuring ongoing communication within the recruitment process. Skills You will have: Excellent intercultural competence, while demonstrating a solid cross-cultural understanding including knowledge and awareness of cultural norms and sensitivities, business etiquette, traditions, and diplomatic protocol; The ability to practice sound judgment and professionalism when working with internal and external partners and stakeholders of diverse backgrounds; The ability to demonstrate a thorough understanding of diverse cultural context and global perspectives; High-level communication skills, including excellent written and oral skills, as well as social media literacy and fluency; Dynamic and energetic public speaking abilities to effectively promote the university brand and concisely explain program offerings, admission pathways, requirements, and processes; The ability to build positive, productive relationships with diverse groups of people, including academic leaders, managers, faculty, staff, future students, and other university stakeholders; Effective team leadership and management skills with the ability to provide direction and subsequently plan, organize, delegate, and evaluate work in collaboration with others; The ability to effectively motivate staff and establish a high-performance team and culture to achieve required goals and outcomes; The ability to perform complex tasks using Microsoft Office Suite customer relationship management software, and student information systems such as PeopleSoft and Business Intelligence; Proven critical thinking, conflict resolution, and collaborative decision-making skills; The ability to collect and analyze applicant and student data to inform evidence-based decisions and evaluate effectiveness of ongoing student recruitment activities and new initiatives with a student experience orientation; Effective problem-solving skills and the ability to make decisions independently in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment; An understanding of International secondary and post-secondary systems with the ability to understand, interpret and apply University policies and procedures, admission requirements, and strategic enrolment management objectives and goals; Knowledge of best practices, initiatives, current research and thinking in student enrolment management, and the ability to assess their relevance and apply within the MacEwan University context; The ability to deal competently and discreetly with sensitive issues; Flexibility to manage multiple tasks and priorities, including the ability to deal with ambiguity and competing demands; and A proven ability to manage special events and projects. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s Degree in International Relations, Education, Business, Administration, or related field. A minimum of 4 years of international recruitment experience and experience with supervising staff. Experience working with students and faculty, as well as developing successful relationships and stakeholder management. A minimum of 2 years of experience working in a post-secondary environment would be considered an asset. Experience studying or living abroad, and proficiency in a language other than English would be considered assets. RCIC or RISIA certification would be considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The ability, willingness, and flexibility to travel and work irregular hours. Must have valid drivers' license and access to a reliable vehicle. Must have valid Canadian passport with the ability to travel internationally and navigate different systems while travelling internationally. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.09.225": {
      "title": "Building and Grounds Supervisor (Internal Only)",
      "description": "Building and Grounds Supervisor (Internal Only) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Building and Grounds Supervisor (Internal Only) Facilities Operations, Infrastructure Planning Management Competition No. 26.09.225 Posting Date September 25, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Replacement Term (35 hours per week) MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). October 9, 2026 Category Full-Time Replacement Term (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band E (Steps 1-8): $32.353 - $47.042 per hour. $58,883 - $85,616 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date October 9, 2026 About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Building and Grounds Supervisor for a full-time 5-month replacement term opportunity with our Facilities Operations department. The Buildings and Grounds Supervisor is responsible for supervising the day-to-day building operations including all general maintenance services as well as the Grounds services at MacEwan University.  Your will be responsible for the supervision of all General Services Facility Maintenance Workers as well all Grounds staff.  This includes staff scheduling, training, and contractor management of contractors providing services to Facilities Operations and ensuring all safe-work practices are followed. Key responsibilities include: Planning, scheduling and implementing various contracted services for grounds planting, grounds equipment repairs, and cosmetic aspects of interior maintenance including minor repairs and upgrades such as painting; Performing monthly audits of quality of contractor work completed, ensuring University standards are being met; Supervising and scheduling Operations Facilities Maintenance Workers (FMW’s) to perform preventative maintenance and to respond to service requests received from the Facilities Information Management System FIMS; Scheduling staff for event set-ups, providing direction and supervision to Custodial staff assisting with event set-ups; Planning and scheduling of Grounds staff to provide a safe and clean campus 7 days per week performing signage and bollard maintenance, graffiti removal, outside garbage collection, lawn care and snow removal; Procuring contractors to perform horticultural work, landscaping projects, planning and enhancing the campus grounds landscaping, flower beds and shrub beds; Maintaining and managing Facilities QMS (Quality Management System) requirements within the General Services and Grounds department; and Holding documented monthly meetings with staff. This opportunity is for internal applicants only. Skills You will have: The ability to perform small engine repairs; Confidence in performing small engine mechanical tasks; The ability to work with FIMS; Working knowledge and familiarity with OHS regulations and codes and the ability to enforce them; Strong interpersonal and communication skills (verbal and written) for the effective management of staff and interactions with University staff, students, and public; Organizational skills that enhance the managerial role of this position while balancing the prioritization of tasks; Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite, PeopleSoft and other applicable programs, as the role requires; The ability to schedule staff and manage hours to maintain budget integrity; Proficiency in identifying facility and grounds needs and scheduling maintenance; The ability to maintain accurate and up-to-date records for maintenance, mitigating liability risk for the University; Capacity for planning and leading meetings for both training and team building; An aptitude for scheduling and monitoring outside contractor work; Sound judgement, follow-through and personal accountability during the entire maintenance process for each task; and The ability to adapt to changing priorities and communicate these changes in a meaningful way to a team of workers. Qualifications A 5 th Class Power Engineering Certificate. Supervisory Development. Grounds horticultural certification. A minimum of 3 years of experience supervising buildings and/or grounds staff. A minimum of 5 years of experience as a building operator or facilities maintenance worker. A minimum of 3 years of experience as a grounds worker. Working knowledge of unionized environments and following collective agreements. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Position Requirements This position is on campus only. The position will participate in an on-call schedule. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.10.246": {
      "title": "Senior Project Manager",
      "description": "Senior Project Manager - Environmental (Internal Only) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Senior Project Manager - Environmental (Internal Only) Infrastructure Planning and Management Competition No. 26.10.246 Posting Date October 7, 2026 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) MSU Band H (Steps 1-8): $46.671 - $67.884 per hour. $84,941 - $123,549 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Continuing (35 hours per week) Salary MSU Band H (Steps 1-8): $46.671 - $67.884 per hour. $84,941 - $123,549 per annum (Based on 35 hours per week). Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 21,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity MacEwan University is seeking a Senior Project Manager – Environmental for a full-time continuing opportunity with the Infrastructure Planning and Management department. Reporting to the Director, Planning and Projects, the Senior Project Manager - Environmental is responsible for leading the strategic development, design and construction of complex and/or high-profile capital building projects, infrastructure improvement projects, and strategic university sponsored projects, valued at up to $200M. You will serve as MacEwan’s internal subject matter expert on environmental regulatory compliance requirements related to the construction of capital building and infrastructure improvement projects and develop and implement processes and practices to ensure ongoing compliance. You will also be a key contributor in the delivery of the university’s master plan. Key responsibilities include: Developing and implementing project management practices for projects with environmental compliance factors, including defining the scope, goals, and success criteria for the project(s); Establishing and maintaining governance processes to ensure effective decision-making and resource allocation; Evaluating progress, identifying risks and issues, and taking corrective actions as needed, which includes providing regular reports and updates to senior management and stakeholders; Identifying, assessing, and managing risks associated with projects that have an environmental impact and/or specific building code requirements; then developing risk mitigation strategies and contingency plans, monitoring and reporting on risk levels, and escalating issues or concerns as necessary; Maintaining full project life cycle ownership: successful project delivery includes full implementation from initiation to deployment for major and/or high-profile initiatives simultaneously; Mentoring and coaching junior team members and sharing knowledge to support continuous learning and development within the team; Employing project management best practices and methods to ensure work is planned and executed to meet applicable University standards, quality, code, regulatory and stakeholder requirements; Developing a project scope statement as the basis for future project decisions, subdividing major deliverables into manageable subset components and implementing effective project control measures to identify variances from plan; Developing and delivering progress reports, proposals, briefing notes, requirements documentation and presentations to various audiences, including project team, sponsors, and key stakeholders; and Ensuring that projects proceed according to scope, schedule, budget, and quality standards. This opportunity is for internal applicants only. Skills You will have: Comprehensive knowledge of Environmental Liability Management and Environment and Protected Areas Guidelines; Comprehensive knowledge of local, provincial and federal environmental standards, regulations and guidelines; A thorough understanding of project and program management principles, methods and techniques; Solid technical understanding and the ability to define and refine requirements through a project lifecycle; A demonstrated ability to problem solve, assess situations, think critically, and apply sound judgment in providing recommendations and making timely and informed choices; Strategic thinking, analytical, problem-solving and decision-making skills with keen attention to detail; A proven ability to act as a positive role model and build trust by consistently demonstrating honesty, integrity, and ethical conduct in all interactions and professional activities; The ability to lead project teams and encourage collaboration; Proven budgetary expertise; Knowledge of change management and process management techniques; The ability to identify, assess and mitigate risks; Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to articulate and present complex subject matter, and effectively engage stakeholders by tailoring the messaging according to the type of audience; Self-motivation with the ability to work independently as well as within a broader team; Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to adapt to change and competing priorities and to meet deadlines; Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; and Demonstrated working knowledge of AutoCAD and project management software such as Microsoft Project and Primavera. Qualifications A minimum of a Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering, Architecture, Environmental Science or Project Management or a related field. Project Management Professional (PMP) certification. Accreditation or eligibility for accreditation with professional governing body in Alberta P.Eng. registered with APEGA), Registered Architect or ASET) is considered an asset. A minimum of 7 years of progressive experience working in project management for architecture, planning, construction contract administration and significant, complex capital building projects and initiatives, including experience in environmental liability management. Experience performing this work in a post-secondary environment is considered an asset. Demonstrated increasing experience in project management (i.e., budgeting, project tracking, and scope control). Experience in contaminated soil sites monitoring and remediation programs. Experience working within and applying local, provincial and federal environmental standards, regulations and guidelines. Experience working in an ISO 9001:2015 environment considered an asset. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Benefits When you become part of the MacEwan University team, you will enjoy a competitive salary. Our total compensation package includes: Competitive base pay Generous vacation time Secure pension plan Flexible benefits package Continuous learning culture Opportunities for career growth How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the MacEwan Staff Union Collective Agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    }
  },
